{"seconds": 90.1, "exit": 0, "final": "After **Nf3+**, White is still up the queen! The White queen on d5 is undefended by the e6 pawn, but White can take the knight, or move the king. White is totally winning.\n\nSo **Qxd5** appears to be the clearly best move\u2014White just wins the Black queen!\n\nLet me verify once more that this is legal and the best continuation:\n\n**Qxd5** wins the Black queen. Black's options are:\n- **exd5**: loses the queen for nothing\n- **Nf3+**: gives check, but White is still up a queen\n\nThis is definitely the answer. The motif is winning a loose piece / taking the hanging piece.\n\n**COACHING NOTE:**\n\nThe Black queen on d5 is undefended after it just moved there with Qxd5. Before recapturing material or making complicated moves, always check if your opponent's last move left a piece hanging. Here, simply capturing the undefended queen with Qxd5 wins decisively. This is a tactical pattern called \"loose piece = lost piece.\"\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qxd5\", \"line\": [\"Qxd5\", \"exd5\"], \"motifs\": [\"hangingPiece\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14", "move": "Bxe5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14", "move": "Qd4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14", "move": "Qd8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14", "move": "Qa4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k2r/pp3ppp/4p3/3qn3/8/8/P1P2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 0 14", "move": "Qb3"}}, {"to